/*!

@page QMMF_Camera_Capture_Request Camera Capture Request

HAL3 Camera works per frame control. Each frame is requested and
configured by Capture request. Multiple streams could be requested in one
Capture request, but configuration is common for all streams in the Capture
request. Configurations are stored in metadata structure. This structure of data
is organized to pairs of tag and corresponding value.

### Capture Request ###

1.  Capture Request consists of metadata and list of stream IDs.
Metadata represents the configuration for requested frames. Capture request
could be applied only on some of the device streams. List of stream IDs
indicates which streams are required for this Capture request.

2.  Camera Adaptor handles device stream and Capture request. It
provides multiple APIs to enhance and simplify work with Capture request:

+   __SubmitCaptureRequestList()__ - Submits a list of Capture requests and
streaming flag. If streaming is enabled Camera Adaptor keeps sending the list of
requests to the Camera until new Capture request, __CancelCaptureRequest__ or
__Flush__ API are called. If streaming is disabled the list of Capture requests
is applied only once. Capture request with streaming mode has lower priority. It
means that non-streaming Capture request will interrupt streaming Capture
requests. The streaming Capture request will be resumed when non-streaming
requests are applied. As an example you can have combination of streaming and
non-streaming Capture request that is capturing image while Video or/and Preview
are running. If Image capture should not interrupt preview and video,
image capture request must include preview and video stream IDs. But in this
case preview and video frame will be generated with snapshot configuration.

+   __SubmitCaptureRequestList__ API returns last frame ID. If Capture request
is streaming, this will return last frame ID from the previous configuration. In
case Capture request is non-streaming this API returns last frame ID for this
Capture request.

+   __CancelCaptureRequest()__ - This is non-blocking API that stops submission
of new Capture requests. The Capture requests that are already submitted in
Camera will be processed.

+   __Flush()__ - This is non-blocking API that aborts Capture requests. If
these requests are already submitted in the Camera, they will be discarded.

+   __WaitUntillIdle()__ - Waits until all buffers from Client and Camera are
returned. If that doesn't happen for the set timeout time this function returns
error. This API is used as a combination of __CancelCaptureRequest__ and
__Flush__ APIs to show when Capture requests are concluded. Then buffers are
processed and returned to stream. After this function is done user can add or
remove device streams.


___
*/